    "notes": "G. de Vahl Davis (1983), Natural convection of air in a square cavity: A bench mark numerical solution. https://doi.org/10.1002/fld.1650030305 . Ra=g*beta*dT*L^3/(nu*alpha)=1e6; L=0.1 m, dT=1 K, rho=1, Cp=1005, beta=1/300 K^-1, nu=4.81840222e-6, alpha=nu/0.71. Transport properties are similarity-scaled inputs, not measured air data. Compare mean hot-wall Nu and centreline velocity extrema after mesh refinement. This is an unvalidated recipe; higher Ra needs finer wall resolution."
